,{"topic":"Benefits","items":[{"id":"Q04810","text":"High rigidity/Low warpage/Temperature resistance","source":"D-FLASH-PBT-GF-TDS-EN","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04811","text":"PBT-GF is a polyester modified material containing 5-10% glass fiber, characterized by temperature resistance, low shrinkage and easy-to-print property, with the ability to be printable on non-heated chamber FFF 3D printers.","source":"D-FLASH-PBT-GF-TDS-EN","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Supports and removal","items":[{"id":"Q04812","text":"If PBT-GF is used as the support material for itself, please remove the support structure as soon as the model cools down.","source":"D-FLASH-PBT-GF-TDS-EN","at":"p. 3","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q04813","text":"Otherwise the support structure can be permanently bonded to the model due to excessive moisture absorption, which will make the support hard to remove.","source":"D-FLASH-PBT-GF-TDS-EN","at":"p. 3","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Printing advice","items":[{"id":"Q04814","text":"After the printing process, it is recommended to dry the model in the oven at 80-100°C for 1-3 hours to increase the strength of the model.","source":"D-FLASH-PBT-GF-TDS-EN","at":"p. 3","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]},{"id":"G132-02","name":"DREMC PBT GF","maker":"DREMC","variant":null,"diameter":"1.75 mm","twins":[],"composition":"PBT with glass fibre under 10 % (\"DREMC PBT GF using BASF Ultradur® PBT resin with added GF <10%\", p. 1, as the sheet states it)","certifications":null,"availability":"End of life for retail: the maker's product page (2026-10-07) says it is replaced by DREMC PC PBT GF, a PC/PBT blend.","claim":null,"values":[{"key":"density","id":"V015024","value":1350,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","page":1,"twin":null,"at":"Density (Physical Properties)"},{"key":"tensileModulusXY","id":"V015031","value":4,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","page":1,"twin":null,"at":"Elastic Modulus (X-Y) (Mechanical Properties)"},{"key":"tensileStrengthXY","id":"V015028","value":70,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","page":1,"twin":null,"at":"Tensile strength(X-Y) (Mechanical Properties)"},{"key":"elongationXY","id":"V015030","value":3,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","page":1,"twin":null,"at":"Elongation at break (X-Y) (Mechanical Properties)"},{"key":"flexuralStrengthXY","id":"V015029","value":110,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","page":1,"twin":null,"at":"Flexural Strength (X-Y) (Mechanical Properties)"},{"key":"hdt045","id":"V015027","value":170,"mark":"counted","why":null,"annealed":null,"source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","page":1,"twin":null,"admitted":["treatment"],"at":"HDT (Physical Properties)"}],"listings":[],"held":[],"replaced":[{"product":"G132-02","key":"density","id":"V015055","value":1350,"by":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","differs":false}],"print":{"nozzle":{"verdict":"within","state":"range","min":260,"max":280,"profileId":"P1914"},"bed":{"verdict":"within","state":"range","min":100,"max":120,"profileId":"P1914"},"chamber":{"verdict":"within-low-end","state":"range","min":60,"max":100,"profileId":"P1914"},"enclosure":"recommended","drying":{"need":"required","c":[null,80],"h":[null,6],"hoursOpen":true,"profileId":"P1912"},"hardened":true,"anneal":[],"advice":null,"from":{},"profileIds":["P1912","P1914"],"fromId":{},"replaced":{"drying":["P1914"]}},"price":null,"notes":[{"topic":"Good for","items":[{"id":"Q07989","text":"Ideal for a variety of applications that demand high-quality printed components such as connectors/switches in automotive applications.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08018","text":"Its has low surface resistant, great for print in place temporarily replacement gears or mostly used for electronic connector housing for its frame resistant rating and chemical/oil resistant.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Benefits","items":[{"id":"Q07962","text":"The has a high temperature resistant with excellent rigidity and tensile strength.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07987","text":"With impressive rigidity, tensile strength, and excellent anti static properties.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07988","text":"This filament is a reliable choice for printing durable and stable parts.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08017","text":"Glass fiber reinforced PBT, known for its excellent chemical resistance and dimensional stability, ideal for parts exposed to harsh environments.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Pitfalls and limitations","items":[{"id":"Q07992","text":"A suitable bed adhesion solution or compatible build plate is required, as this material does not adhere well to most standard bed adhesives and build plates.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08005","text":"Do not print on bare PEI without bed adhesive barrier","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Warping and shrinkage","items":[{"id":"Q07986","text":"Its <10% glass fibre composition provides exceptional heat resistance and minimal shrinkage.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07993","text":"at least 60-90c minimal active/passive chamber is recommended, our recommendation is 80-100c+, to reduce warping/material shrinkage during printing on complex parts.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Moisture sensitivity","items":[{"id":"Q07964","text":"DREMC PBT GF print from dry box or dryer.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07965","text":"This material easily absorbs moisture.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07966","text":"If the filament becomes wet, it is recommended to dry it in a hot air oven at 80°C for at least 6 hours to ensure the success rate and quality of the printed model.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07996","text":"For best results, dry filament using a filament drier before use and print from dryer running or dry box.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07997","text":"Keep in an airtight container or included mylar bag for medium/long term storage with silica desiccant.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07998","text":"If you hear popping or inconsistent extrusion while purging filament, suggest drying before printing for best results","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08011","text":"~80 ° c for 8-12hr","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08012","text":"Only dry if filament is wet, over drying/repeat drying can damage filament","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08013","text":"Keeping filament in an airtight container or provided Mylar bag with new/dried desiccant .","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Nozzle wear","items":[{"id":"Q07994","text":"Abrasive resistance nozzle is requirement due to glass fibre, plated/brass nozzle can wear quickly and cause inconsistent prints and will destroy those types of nozzles.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07995","text":"A wear resistant nozzle must be used, carbon fiber material is abrasive and will wear standard brass nozzles and >0.5mm nozzle is recommended.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Odour and emissions","items":[{"id":"Q07999","text":"At temperatures above >290°C can and may emitted: carbon monoxide, tetrahydrofuran.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08000","text":"Material is stable up to 280°C and do not give rise to hazards due to molecular degradation or the evolution of gases and vapors.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08002","text":"Always print in an enclosed setup with active exhaust, and make sure your workspace is equipped with a carbon monoxide sensor for added safety.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08009","text":"Recommend VOC/Air Filtering/fume extraction or print in well ventilated room with fume extraction.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Supports and removal","items":[{"id":"Q07967","text":"If using PBT GF as a support material, it's advisable to remove the support structures as soon as the model has cooled.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07968","text":"If the model absorbs moisture, the support structures may adhere to the model, making them difficult to remove.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]},{"topic":"Printing advice","items":[{"id":"Q07963","text":"You may see better mechanical properties once annealed","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07969","text":"Annealing Tip: 80-100 °C for 2-3 hours.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07990","text":"This material is highly recommended for tool changer/IDEX printers.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q07991","text":"For better bed adhesion and to reduce warping, it is best to use PC ABS, ABS, or PC(similar material blend) for the first couples layer or support raft.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08001","text":"Ensure your hotend is accurately temperature-calibrated, and do not exceed the recommended printing temperature of 280°C.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08003","text":"Works well with most common build surfaces.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08004","text":"We recommended PEI Build Plate (Smooth/Textured) with Bed Adhesive such as Glue Stick / Magigoo HT.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08006","text":"LOW-MEDIUM for better surface quality OFF-LOW (<10%) for better strength","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08007","text":"Recommended for complex larger geometries.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08008","text":"60-100˚C+ may be required for higher density and larger geometries.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08010","text":"<60mm/s is our recommendation for most pro-consumer hardware","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08014","text":"Due to the low co-efficient of friction please ensure you have smooth filament path from filament box/dryer.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08015","text":"We recommended 3x4mm PTFE to be used for reverse bowden.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"},{"id":"Q08016","text":"As always you should do temperature to tower as each machine printing temperature may vary depending on hotend/printing speed etc.","source":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","at":"p. 1","domain":"Makers' know-how","type":"Manufacturer statement"}]}]}],"layers":[],"published":[{"property":"Fibre content","domain":"physical","unit":"%","products":2,"lo":5,"hi":10,"median":8.75,"values":[7.5,10]},{"property":"Melt mass-flow rate","domain":"physical","unit":"g/10 min","products":2,"lo":15,"hi":20,"median":16.25,"values":[15,17.5]},{"property":"Water absorption","domain":"physical","unit":"%","products":2,"lo":0.4,"hi":0.4,"median":0.4,"values":[0.4,0.4]}],"environment":[],"guide":null,"resin":null,"sources":[{"id":"D-FLASH-PBT-GF-TDS-EN","publisher":"Flashforge","title":"Technical Data Sheet PBT-GF Filament","date":null,"read":"2026-09-19","kind":"Manufacturer TDS","url":"https://after-support.flashforge.jp/uploads/datasheet/tds/PBT_GF_TDS_EN.pdf"},{"id":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-70f515d2b287","publisher":"DREMC","title":"PBT GF – Glass Fibre Technical Data Sheet (TDS)","date":null,"read":"2026-10-07","kind":"Manufacturer TDS","url":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0541/6638/8905/files/DREMC_PBT_GF_TDS_V1.1.pdf?v=1747390078","revision":"V1.1","note":"DREMC's three-page data sheet for its PBT GF filament (file DREMC_PBT_GF_TDS_V1.1.pdf, linked from the product page): physical and mechanical tables, the test bars' printing conditions, a drying note."},{"id":"R-DREMC-QR-20261007-a23be9ad12ed","publisher":"DREMC","title":"DREMC PBT GF Glass Fibre Filament 1.75mm 1kg","date":null,"read":"2026-10-07","kind":"Manufacturer product page or guide","url":"https://store.dremc.com.au/products/dremc-pbt-gf-glass-fibre-filament-1-75mm-1kg","revision":"Product page as served on 2026-10-07","note":"DREMC's own product page for PBT GF: its specification block (density) and its printing settings and requirements (nozzle, bed, chamber, drying, a wear-resistant nozzle). The page marks the product end of life for retail."}]}